title: harbour_gate
---
<<declare $knows_about_key = false>>
<<declare $knows_boats_lost = false>>
<<declare $tam_trusts_player = false>>
// Dawn. Fog sits on the water. MARGOT, the harbour keeper, is mending a net and does not look up. Plays when the player first arrives.
MARGOT: You've come down the salt road. Nobody does that any more. #line:MARGOT_001
-> I need to reach the lighthouse.
    MARGOT: Then you need the key, and the key is with Tam. #line:MARGOT_002
    <<set $knows_about_key to true>>
    <<jump net_loft>>
-> Why is the harbour empty?
    MARGOT: The boats went out after the light went dark. None came back. #line:MARGOT_003
    <<set $knows_boats_lost to true>>
    <<jump harbour_gate>>
-> Never mind.
    <<stop>>
    // BARK MARGOT_004 MARGOT: Mind the wet planks.
    // BARK MARGOT_005 MARGOT: Fog is thicker than it was.
    // LORE: The salt road runs along the bar at low water. It is dry for four hours a day, and not one minute more.
===

title: net_loft
---
// A loft of drying nets. TAM, young and out of breath, hides a brass key behind his back.
TAM: Margot sent you? She always sends someone. They never come back. #line:TAM_001
-> The boats never came back either. I know. <<if $knows_boats_lost>>
    TAM: Then you know why I am scared of that light. #line:TAM_002
    <<set $tam_trusts_player to true>>
    <<jump lighthouse_door>>
-> Give me the key.
    TAM: Take it. Please. Just take it. #line:TAM_003
    <<jump lighthouse_door>>
-> I will leave you to it.
    <<jump harbour_gate>>
    // BARK TAM_004 TAM: Is somebody there?
===

title: lighthouse_door
---
// The tide is already lapping at the steps. The door is stiff, and the lamp room above is dark.
<<if $tam_trusts_player>>TAM: I will hold the door. Go on. #line:TAM_005<<endif>>
-> Climb to the lamp room.
    <<stop>>
-> Turn back.
    <<jump net_loft>>
===
